#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:82
msgid "Tables Actions"
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:83
msgid "Actions available for each table depend on the table and what plugin settings allow."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:85
msgid "Optimize and Repair options are available if table should be optimized, or if the table has crashed and broken. Both these actions will essentially run the Sweepers."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:86
msgid "After optimization, it is possible that table still shows as not optimized, and that is either because server is unable to finish optimization in best way, or the server statistics is not updated in time, and this is normal behavior for the InnoDB tables."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:87
msgid "Repairing tables usually works without issues, but in some cases, repair is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:88
msgid "Some tables will be displayed differently and color coded based on their status."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:90
msgid "Database Backup"
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:91
msgid "Some of the actions on this page can be dangerous to use."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:93
msgid "Truncate and Drop actions are available only if enabled in the plugin settings, and they can be run only on some database tables. Both these actions will destroy database data, and the operations are final, and will require special approval each time."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:94
msgid "If you use any of these by accident, the only way to get your data back would be with backup. Make sure to have backup ready before using any of these actions!"
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:102
msgid "This panel shows all the unique meta keys in the metadata table. For each meta key, you will get number of times this key is used, how much space its values take, and how big the values for the key are on average. Most important information is the status and source for the meta key. Based on the detected source, plugin will determine the status of the key."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:104
msgid "All meta keys found in the metadata table are displayed, including WordPress based meta keys."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:105
msgid "Meta keys that are detected as installed and active (belonging to plugin or theme) and meta keys belonging to WordPress, will not have Delete option included."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:107
msgid "SweepPress uses several methods to determine the source for all the meta keys inside the metadata table. It is important to know few thing about this process."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:110
msgid "To determine which plugin or theme owns or uses the meta key, plugin uses regular expressions with predefined values, and the scanner to find these settings in the plugin or theme source code."
msgstr ""

