#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:162
msgid "When it comes to Multisite installations, there are some specific rules."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:116
msgid "Usermeta table will not show the 'Active' or 'Inactive' status flags."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:116
#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:164
msgid "The reason for this is that in Multisite plugins can be active on some blogs only, but usermeta table is shared, and one blog can't know what plugins are used on other blogs (well, they can, but that will be very system performance intensive operation to run, especially on big networks)."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:123
#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:124
msgid "Metadata Preview"
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:125
msgid "This panel shows all individual metadata records for the selected meta key, linked to the main object record. Every record here can be deleted individually, or using bulk deletion."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:127
msgid "Value column will attempt to show the actual stored value. But, if the value is serialized PHP array or object, or serialized JSON object, the direct preview is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:128
msgid "To have full preview for such data, you need a free plugin called `DebugPress`, and there is an option in the Settings to enable this integration."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:129
msgid "If these records don't show the reference object relation, that means that record is orphaned. To remove all orphaned records all at once, SweepPress has sweepers for this very purpose."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:138
msgid "From this panel you can manage various metadata database tables."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:140
msgid "All default WordPress metadata tables are supported and listed here: `commentmeta`, `postmeta`, `termmeta`, `usermeta` and `blogmeta`. coreActivity `logmeta` table is also supported."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:141
msgid "Data and information presented on these panels is cached with 2 hours cache interval. Queries that deal with these tables can be very slow when used with big database tables."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:149
msgid "This panel shows the options available in the WordPress `Sitemeta` database table with some exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:155
msgid "SweepPress uses several methods to determine the source for the options inside the WordPress Sitemeta database table. It is important to know few thing about this process."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:158
msgid "To determine which plugin owns settings in the Sitemeta table, plugin uses regular expressions with predefined values, and the scanner to find these settings in the plugin or theme source code."
msgstr ""

#: core/pro/admin/Help.php:164
msgid "Sitemeta table will not show the 'Active' or 'Inactive' status flags."
msgstr ""

